From 71448f63ba189b1f61153e7df766f9421b350205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:38:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Carry the explicit local verifier through the relay, native
 issuer and host-service launch boundaries

ENCLAVE_CHAIN_AUTHORITY=verifier + ENCLAVE_CHAIN_VERIFIER (loopback) now reach the readers that
sit behind a filtered or rebuilt child configuration:

- measured guest: platformApi.relayEnv validates the pair at bind time; the relay child's
  environment (relayChildEnv) carries exactly the bound pair - a sealed credential can neither
  set nor change it - and the native issuer's host policy reads the same bound env.
- api-relay: the network LeaseReader takes its authority from networkReaderOptions(env)
  (relay/chain-sources.mjs); verifier mode passes no RPC list, so no provider client exists.
  A verifier without ADDRESS_BOOK_ADDRESS, a remote URL or a runtime bundle without the
  verifier authority stops the relay. The startup log states the authority and tier.
- dns-relay: the app-zone LeaseReader and the Shield host-identity registry reader follow the
  same env (Shield via LeaseReader's agreed(), same interface as quorumReader); the runtime
  bundle exports chainAuthorityFromEnv and networkReaderOptions.
- challenge replica: chainAuthority/chainVerifier reach the host policy gate env, the runner
  carrier shape and the dns-relay child env; chain.rpcs / shield.rpcs optional only then; a
  verifier no chain read would use is refused.
- host-services directory-replica role: chainAuthority/chainVerifier pass the role filter into
  directory-server's config (rpc optional only then); directory-server logs its authority.
- native-profile: --chain-verifier (and an input profile's pair) drive its own lease reads and
  are emitted into the profile the NativeClient later uses.

The provider quorum stays the default everywhere; explicit verifier failures refuse.
